{"timestamp": 1779430121.8979437, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 13, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "weapons", "victim_name": "Diana"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779430121.8993323, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 13, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430131.2741623, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I just found Diana's body in Weapons. I was moving around trying to get my tasks done\u2014my route was Cafeteria to Medbay, then Electrical, back up through Cafeteria, and finally over to Weapons. I honestly didn't cross paths with a single person the entire time, so I didn't see anyone leaving the scene. \n\nSince I didn't see anyone on the right side of the map, the killer must have vented or went down towards Security/Navigation. Where was everyone else? Did anyone see someone heading towards or coming from the top right?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430138.0646293, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I was on the complete opposite side of the map the whole time. I started in Oxygen, went down to Upper Engine, and I was just in Lower Engine when the body was reported. I haven't crossed paths with a single person all round, which checks out if all the movement was happening over on the right side near Weapons. I can't really help pinpoint anyone unfortunately, but at least you know the left side was clear. Let's hear where Bob, Charlie, and Eve were."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430149.9680028, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Listen up, I have a very strong lead. Frank finding Diana in Weapons makes total sense. My route was Weapons, down to Security, and then to Navigation. \n\nRight at the start of the round, I was in Weapons. Bob walked in from Security, and a couple of seconds later, Diana came in from Security too. When I left Weapons to head south, I left Bob and Diana alone together in that room. If she was killed there and Frank didn't see anyone passing through Cafeteria, Bob is almost certainly our killer. \n\nBob, you have a lot of explaining to do. What exactly happened in Weapons after I left?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430163.504933, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I can confirm that the left and bottom sides of the map were completely dead. I started in Lower Engine, went through Storage, and ended up in Medbay just now. I didn't cross paths with a single person all round. I missed Alice since I moved out of Lower Engine early on. \n\nSince Frank, Alice, and I practically saw nobody, it makes perfect sense that all the movement was concentrated on the right side of the ship. \n\nEve, that is a very specific and damning accusation. If what you're saying is true, Bob is absolutely our Duck. It's a hard accuse, which usually means it's either the truth or a very bold Duck play. \n\nBob, you have the last word. You'd better have a flawless explanation for what happened in Weapons, or I'm throwing my vote your way based on Eve's testimony. Let's hear it."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430199.6116726, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Eve\u2019s framing is leaving out the important timing. Yes, I was in Weapons early, and yes, Diana came in after me from Security. Eve was there too. But I did **not** stay there with Diana for the whole round.\n\nWhat happened from my side: I came up from Security into Weapons, saw Eve there, then Diana came in. Eve left down toward Security. I stayed only briefly, then I left Weapons **up/left through Cafeteria**, went Medbay, then Upper Engine, where I was when the report got called. Diana was alive in Weapons when I left.\n\nSo Eve saying \u201cI left Bob and Diana alone, therefore Bob killed\u201d is a huge leap. She\u2019s the one who was on that right-side route and admits being in Weapons/Security/Navigation. If she doubled back from Security to Weapons after I left, nobody would\u2019ve seen it, especially since Frank says he saw nobody on his route.\n\nI get why it looks bad because I was seen with Diana, but I\u2019m telling you: I left her alive in Weapons. Eve is making this sound way more certain than it actually is."}}
{"timestamp": 1779430211.0362566, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430225.84192, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430233.3856835, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430303.4183445, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Bob"}}
{"timestamp": 1779430321.565867, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Hold on, everyone piling \u201cBob\u201d off one testimony is exactly how we lose to a clean frame.\n\nEve\u2019s story proves I was in Weapons early, not that I killed Diana. She left Weapons before me. Diana was alive when I left. I went Cafeteria \u2192 Medbay \u2192 Upper Engine, which is why Alice can place the left side quiet and I wasn\u2019t anywhere near the body when Frank found it.\n\nThe person with the easiest opportunity to make this accusation is Eve: she admits she was Weapons \u2192 Security \u2192 Navigation, meaning she was right under the body area and could\u2019ve doubled back to Weapons with nobody seeing, especially since everyone else is saying they saw nobody. Then she hard-accuses me because she knows I was the last person she personally saw with Diana.\n\nFrank also says he came through Cafeteria to Weapons and saw nobody, which fits me having left earlier, not me hanging around after a kill.\n\nIf you vote me here, you\u2019re voting purely on \u201cBob was once in the same room,\u201d not on who could\u2019ve actually returned unseen. I think Eve is pushing way too hard on a convenient story."}}
